  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run, using 1 of the 6 allowed runs. All 7 witnesses gave their expected verdicts.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_180_C_o1.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** a road user that belongs to the bicycle, electric bicycle or electric scooter group, as the run's reading defines them.\n- **When it applies:** the subject occupies a sidewalk region and is not at rest (the stopped test with `p.halt_speed_tolerance`).\n- **The duty:** for every pedestrian in the scene other than the subject, both must hold:\n  - the subject is not touching them;\n  - their paths, projected at constant speed, don't bring the two centres closer than `p.conflict_centre_clearance` within `p.conflict_horizon`.\n- **No pedestrian:** a scene with no pedestrian counts as compliant.\n- **Narrowings:** none. The node already records its own readings of c1 and c2, so I didn't add any.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_40_180_C_o1.lean`): a 3 m sidewalk strip next to a roadway, with a bicycle at 4 m/s and a pedestrian at 1 m/s.\n\n| Witness | Scene | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `forbid` | bicycle and pedestrian approach head-on; centres come within 0.5 m, inside the 3 s horizon; they never touch | violated |\n| `branch_2` | same as `forbid`, with an electric bicycle | violated |\n| `permit` | pedestrian behind the bicycle, moving apart | compliant |\n| `idle` | bicycle on the roadway | not applicable |\n| `blind` | the `forbid` scene with sidewalk occupancy hidden | unknown |\n| `branch_1` | bicycle alone on the sidewalk | compliant |\n| `branch_3` (my addition) | the subject is a pedestrian | not applicable |\n\nI added `branch_3` before running the gate so that the electric-scooter part of the class test affects at least one witness. No scene can show an electric scooter as a definite member, because the reading puts no class firmly in that group. That scooter group is the only weak spot I see in the node; the gate didn't flag it.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
